      "id": 239257,
      "name": "KateWalker",
      "username": "TakeWalker",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/takewalker/{size}/5677_2.png",
      "created_at": "2021-07-13T15:58:57.532Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Ooh, Head Doctor! I know it’s their own canon, but that’s a deep cut!</p>\n<p>I love that everything in this story hinges on ‘radio waves’ and they trap a villain’s mind in a radio. This is so goofy, I’m just so impressed by their ability to transgress the timelines like this. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=9\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\"> This was a very satisfying Wrtiers’ Room.</p>\n<p>I like a body-swap story where the villain is all, “Exchanging my mind for the hero’s so I can use their powers in my latest scheme is <em>so</em> much easier than trying to trick them into helping me!” and then when they’re ready to swap back, the hero’s like, no, are you kidding, you live in this opulent mansion, you’re good-looking, I don’t have people clamoring for me to save them, <em>you</em> go be the hero, I’m gonna enjoy this!</p>\n<p>Funny how that BPW letter got them into a real “who would win?” discussion.</p>\n<p>And that cover is just the icing on the cheesy silver age cake. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=9\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\"></p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-07-13T15:59:22.186Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
