      "username": "The_Justifier",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_justifier/{size}/4954_2.png",
      "created_at": "2021-07-14T00:19:24.377Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Not much, but at the same time so very critically much indeed.  Normally she’s almost pure white, with just a couple thin lines and circles of red, which create a visible solid-red blur behind her, but not so much on her.  The big clown-nose red spots on the cover are so much more garish, it’s extremely obvious to me (plus the extra red on the boots and things).  Obviously in the 60s she couldn’t have the bare shoulder, but otherwise I think the costume would have been better off staying very close to its modern look.</p>",
